% M7-T22 / D-0086 (b): A ROOT REFUTATION THE CHECKER REJECTED, from M7-T21's random sweep
% (`bench/fuzz/gen.py ad 24319`, shrunk greedily; ad 25012 is the same shape). FIXED; an
% ordinary passing model test whose proof is verified on every run.
%
% THE DEFECT. x3 is both an element RESULT and in the all_different scope. Regin punches
% an interior hole in x3, and that removal's explanation concluded the DIRECT literal
% ~x3_eq_v, while every other hole in the store -- and the hole's own trace line -- is the
% ORDER clause ~x3_ge_v \/ x3_ge_(v+1). Element's [excl_hole] embeds the remover's
% explanation and pairs it off against two order-literal rows; handed the direct literal,
% nothing cancelled, the root conflict's row kept its literals, and 3.0.2 answered "The
% constraint with ID n is not contradicting, as specified by the hint" at the
% `conclusion` line (line 112 of the unshrunk seed).
%
% THE FIX is alldiff.ml's [in_order_currency]: an interior Regin removal adds its value's
% forward channelling line, divisor 1, and concludes the order clause. No SAT twin: the
% defect is in a root conflict's closing row (a scratch search of 20 000 SAT-biased
% all_different + element models found no instance under a decision). The break is a
% REFUSAL, so D-0066's vacuity cannot hide it; measured on the binary of the (c) commit,
% rejected at line 43, `conclusion UNSAT : @c<n> ;`.
var 4..5: x0 :: output_var;
var 1..1: x1 :: output_var;
var 2..4: x3 :: output_var;
var 3..5: x4 :: output_var;
constraint all_different_int([x3,x0,x4,x1]);
constraint array_int_element(x4,[2,5,3,4,2],x3);
constraint int_lin_le([2,-1],[x4,x0],1);
solve :: int_search([x0,x4,x1,x3], smallest, indomain_max, complete) satisfy;
